   7:  * never repeated per suite. What stays in a suite is scenario evidence: no-fault control runs,
   8:  * mid-flight-not-yet-delivered checks, meaningful-config guards, role-actually-moved checks.
   9:  *
  10:  * LOAD-BEARING, and the reason these have conformance tests of their own: a bug in a centralized
  11:  * guard green-lights all thirty suites at once. A fault handle that counted "armed" as "triggered"
  12:  * would make every atomicity test in the product pass on nothing at all, and no suite would show
  13:  * a symptom. H3 (sentinels + fault injection) MUST route its `sentinels.plant`, `faults.at`,
